# Git MUST NOT rewrite any byte in this repository.
#
# On Windows, git converts LF to CRLF on checkout by default. A TCC signature is
# computed over the RAW BYTES of `manifest.json`, and the content hash over the
# raw bytes of every file in `content/` — so a helpful line-ending conversion
# adds one byte per line and destroys every signature in the repository.
#
# This is not hypothetical. `tcc verify examples/hello-tcc` passed on macOS and
# Linux and failed on Windows with "chữ ký Ed25519 không hợp lệ", the first time
# CI ran there. The package was never broken; the checkout was.
#
# `-text` on everything, not just on packages: a rule that has to be remembered
# for each new signed file is a rule that gets forgotten the day somebody adds
# one.
* -text

# Conformance vectors are compared byte for byte against expected hashes, so
# they are in the same position as package content.
conformance/vectors/*.json -text

# Fuzzing corpora are opaque bytes by definition.
fuzz/seeds/** -text binary
